::__construct} — Create Swoole sync or async TCP/UDP client, with or without SSL.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::__destruct} — Destruct the Swoole client.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::getpeername} — Get the remote socket name of the connection.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::getsockname} — Get the local socket name of the connection.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::isConnected} — Check if the connection is established.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::on} — Add callback functions triggered by events.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::pause} — Pause receiving data.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::pipe} — Redirect the data to another file descriptor.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::recv} — Receive data from the remote socket.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::resume} — Resume receiving data.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::send} — Send data to the remote TCP socket.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::sendfile} — Send file to the remote TCP socket.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::sendto} — Send data to the remote UDP address.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::set} — Set the Swoole client parameters before the connection is established.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::sleep} — Remove the TCP client from system event loop.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Client::wakeup} — Add the TCP client back into the system event loop.</li></ul></div>
